[TITLE]
An outfall carrying BOTH a flap gate and a Route To subcatchment.

Legacy reads those two trailing columns with exact token-count equality —
`ntoks == n` assigns the flap gate, `ntoks == n+1` assigns RouteTo
(node.c outfall_readParams) — so the combination cannot be expressed in the
SWMM 5.x grammar at all: a legacy engine reading a file with both silently
takes RouteTo and defaults the gate to NO.

O_BOTH has both and must raise a writer warning. O_GATE has only the gate and
must not.

[OPTIONS]
FLOW_UNITS           CFS
INFILTRATION         HORTON
FLOW_ROUTING         DYNWAVE
START_DATE           01/01/2024
END_DATE             01/01/2024
REPORT_STEP          00:15:00
ROUTING_STEP         00:00:30

[RAINGAGES]
RG1  INTENSITY  0:05  1.0  TIMESERIES TS1

[TIMESERIES]
TS1  0:00  0.0
TS1  1:00  0.5

[SUBCATCHMENTS]
;;Name  RainGage  Outlet  Area  %Imperv  Width  %Slope  CurbLen
S_RECV  RG1       J1      1.0   25.0     100.0  0.5     0

[SUBAREAS]
S_RECV  0.013  0.1  0.05  0.05  25  OUTLET

[INFILTRATION]
S_RECV  3.0  0.5  4.0  7  0

[JUNCTIONS]
;;Name  Elev   MaxDepth
J1      100.0  10.0
J2      99.0   10.0

[OUTFALLS]
;;Name  Elev  Type  Stage  Gated  RouteTo
O_BOTH  90.0  FREE         YES    S_RECV
O_GATE  90.0  FREE         YES

[CONDUITS]
;;Name  From  To      Length  Rough  InOff  OutOff
C1      J1    J2      100.0   0.013  0      0
C2      J2    O_BOTH  100.0   0.013  0      0
C3      J2    O_GATE  100.0   0.013  0      0

[XSECTIONS]
C1  CIRCULAR  1.5  0  0  0  1
C2  CIRCULAR  1.5  0  0  0  1
C3  CIRCULAR  1.5  0  0  0  1

[COORDINATES]
J1      0    0
J2      100  0
O_BOTH  200  0
O_GATE  200  100

[Polygons]
S_RECV  0  0
S_RECV  0  50
S_RECV  50 50
